00:28:03.280 --> 00:28:08.280
<v Matt Young>it, you talked about it, you can iterate on the solution and you're on your way to success.

352
00:28:08.740 --> 00:28:13.240
<v Matt Young>If you just have a solution and haven't really vetted the product, take a step back. There are

353
00:28:13.240 --> 00:28:19.020
<v Matt Young>more problems out there to solve than there are people to solve them. So go for it. You'll be

354
00:28:19.020 --> 00:28:21.820
<v Matt Young>successful despite yourself if something is wrong.

355
00:28:22.440 --> 00:28:24.920
<v Noah Labhart>That's great advice. Well, Matt, thanks for being

356
00:28:24.920 --> 00:28:25.620
<v Noah Labhart>on the show today.

